.TH PRINTENV "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
printenv \- print all or part of environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B printenv
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR] [\fI\,VARIABLE\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Print the values of the specified environment VARIABLE(s).
If no VARIABLE is specified, print name and value pairs for them all.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#printenv-0'\fB\-0, \-\-null\fP\X'tty: link'
end each output line with NUL, not newline
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/printenv#printenv--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/printenv#printenv--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
.PP
Your shell may have its own version of printenv, which usually supersedes
the version described here.  Please refer to your shell's documentation
for details about the options it supports.
